WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.520
- Sony just isn't stopping

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.330
when it comes to new
camera releases this year.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.250
This is one that I'm
really excited to show you

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.310
because right now,

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.500
this is the world's smallest,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.100
lightest, full frame camera body,

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.873
with interchangeable lenses
and this new color option.

00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:15.859
(indistinct)

00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:18.442
(upbeat music)

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.770
This is the all new
Sony a7C Compact Camera.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.670
This is actually an entirely
new category for Sony,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.320
is the compact camera line.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.860
Now this camera is full frame.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.900
Starting price is 1799 for the body

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.900
and 2099 with an all new 20
to 60 millimeter F4 zoom lens.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.860
They're also coming out

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:41.970
with some new, smaller,

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:43.600
compact lenses to go with this.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.900
Because this is so light,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.500
you wanna have a nice
light lens to go with it.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.290
I know that it's incredibly overwhelming,

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.510
the amount of cameras out there,

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:52.720
especially just in the Sony family,

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.470
but when creators start
looking for that real first

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:57.260
mirrorless camera to upgrade to,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.760
I'm so excited that this is now an option.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.920
What's the lowest cost
I can get for a camera

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.990
without sacrificing too many features?

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.140
Is a question that I get so often.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:08.010
And I'm always on the
hunt for that answer.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:10.010
I used to make a ton of travel content

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:11.730
and the camera that I would mostly use

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.820
was the Sony a6500,

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:16.010
but this would have been the camera

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.330
that I would have gravitated towards,

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.480
if this was out back then.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.660
Now I know that the new Sony
a7S is coming out very soon,

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.610
and that will be my main camera of choice,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.300
but that camera is very expensive

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.310
and it is a higher end production camera.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:28.730
And it's not for everyone.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.030
We almost always have a
second camera on shoots,

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:33.100
and because this is so light,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:35.690
this is going to be
perfect to put on a Ronin

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:36.950
or to use on our lower sliders,

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.830
or even just to use as a second
off camera angle like this.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.000
Let's also just come back to the fact

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.660
that this is a full frame camera.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:48.680
A lot of the previous mirrorless
cost efficient cameras have

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.410
the smaller APS sensor.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.840
So this will let you
use full frame lenses,

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.290
and this will significantly
improve your photo

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.750
or video quality, especially
when shooting in low light.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.800
And

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.030
have I showed you this?

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.430
It's got the flip out screen.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:05.160
This is something that is
going to make everyone's lives

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.510
so much easier.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.650
This was the one deciding factor of why

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:11.320
a lot of people ended up
not getting a Sony camera,

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.690
is because when you are
vlogging and filming yourself,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:16.200
being able to have that
flip out screen is amazing.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.100
Now they tried to compensate
for that by the 6400

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.510
having a flip up screen.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.140
But when you have a camera
that has interchangeable lenses

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.000
and a hot shoe for audio,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.560
you're gonna wanna put
a microphone on this.

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.440
And when you put a microphone
on this flip up screen,

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.359
just take a guess what happened?

00:02:32.359 --> 00:02:33.192
(camera thuds on the table)

00:02:33.192 --> 00:02:34.025
Spoiler alert.

00:02:34.025 --> 00:02:34.858
You couldn't see the screen.

00:02:34.858 --> 00:02:36.170
Thankfully, a lot of these cameras

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.720
do have really good onboard audio,

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.890
so it wasn't always necessary to have.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:44.110
When that with a7S III with a
flip out screen was announced,

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:44.943
(Justine's hand thud on the table)

00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:45.850
that's it, it's a game changer.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.137
Now the size comparison is

00:02:47.137 --> 00:02:49.170
what I really wanna show you guys.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.700
This is the Sony a7 III,

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.230
this is what I pretty much use right now

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.560
for shooting everything.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.737
In between there is the smaller sensor,

00:02:57.737 --> 00:02:59.820
the Sony a6400.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.250
So here they all are side by side.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.760
And the biggest thing
about this is the fact

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.250
that this is a new compact form factor,

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.500
as opposed to a 7 III.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.640
So the a7S III is a little
more like this form factor,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.580
it is heavier.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.450
So they've also moved the lens
piece over here to the left,

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.560
so it doesn't mimic more of the a6400

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.310
and more in this alpha line.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.220
This just feels so huge at this point.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.320
I mean, you guys can see

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.260
the size difference in the sensor here.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.060
I also really like the
new body that they have

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.560
for this compact camera,

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.660
this silver kind of reminds me more

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:34.230
of like a vintage camera,

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.700
but it just looks slick,

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:36.533
it looks updated.

00:03:36.533 --> 00:03:38.350
This looks like a real 2020,

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.930
well, don't say it looks like 2020,

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.780
but I'm just saying like
a camera up at the time,

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.740
like an updated look.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.080
A nice new modern feel.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.650
It almost kind of looks
like a carbon fiber finish.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.750
This does also come in
a black version as well,

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.180
but I really do like the silver.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.270
I think a lot of people
are going to be into that.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.620
Do you like the silver?
- [Tyler] Yeah!

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.560
- Tyler's into it.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.060
It's cool.
- [Tyler] You know why?

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.788
- 'Cause it looks like an
old film camera, right?

00:03:58.788 --> 00:03:59.950
(laughing together)

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:01.160
Jenna is FaceTiming me.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:02.530
Oh my God, is it an emergency?

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.660
It's gotta be an emergency.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.950
Hello?

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.320
- [Jenna] What are we
gonna do about the podcast?

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:07.691
- What's wrong?

00:04:07.691 --> 00:04:08.640
Do you maybe see this before?

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:09.473
- [Jenna] Oh my God,

00:04:09.473 --> 00:04:10.306
yeah, it's nice.

00:04:10.306 --> 00:04:11.910
I used it, it's crispy.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.100
What do you think of where
that menu button is located?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.348
- Oh, menu button?

00:04:15.348 --> 00:04:16.181
(phone beeps)

00:04:16.181 --> 00:04:18.360
That was a really great chat.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.810
I like that they moved
the menu button right here

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:20.643
to the center,

00:04:20.643 --> 00:04:22.400
look, if you can't find the menu button,

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.880
you're definitely not looking hard enough.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.663
Oh, menu button.

00:04:28.142 --> 00:04:30.725
(upbeat music)

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.080
So the headphone jack, we have USB-C,

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.760
micro HTMI, SD card slot,

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:38.240
and a microphone input.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.970
The a7S III does have an
all new updated menu system.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:43.070
This one does not, unfortunately,

00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.670
because that menu system is really,

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:45.820
really cool.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:48.413
Someone is cutting grass.

00:04:48.413 --> 00:04:51.080
(machinery whirring in the background)

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.270
Here's where the battery goes.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.630
And boy, am I excited that they decided

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.220
to cut the grass right now.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:00.090
So this will shoot 4K, 30 and 24.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.790
And in 1080 you can do 24, 30,

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.420
60, and 120.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:04.690
This also has S and Q,

00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:05.740
which we use a lot,

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.620
especially for doing time
lapses or slow motion videos.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.600
It'll automatically
perform them into a video.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.660
So you don't have to be
messing with a bunch of photos

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.600
to create a time lapse,

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:15.960
it will do it all automatically
for you in camera.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:16.860
So this is the old battery,

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:17.693
and this is the new ones,

00:05:17.693 --> 00:05:18.540
this is the Z-series.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.560
And this thing is so much better

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:21.890
than these older, smaller ones.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:24.810
We would go through so many
batteries during a day,

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.300
that I probably have 45 of these.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.160
Crazy.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:28.993
The good thing though,

00:05:28.993 --> 00:05:32.140
is at some point during
my a7S II shooting days,

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.480
I got one of the AC adapters
and that's been amazing.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:37.430
But now with this and
some of the newer cameras,

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:38.460
like the A7 III that we're using,

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:39.550
and the new a7S III,

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.060
you can actually power
those through USB-C,

00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.660
and that is just,

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.493
I mean.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.930
incredible.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.689
♪ Smiling to some strangers ♪

00:05:48.689 --> 00:05:50.672
♪ Swinging on my feet ♪

00:05:50.672 --> 00:05:54.710
♪ Then I see the moonlights
sparkling in your eyes ♪

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:59.710
♪ All my body's frozen
and my soul's on fire ♪

00:05:59.784 --> 00:06:04.129
♪ Just follow me baby ♪

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:08.051
♪ Pulling at me with a foxy move ♪

00:06:08.051 --> 00:06:09.490
♪ I gently come over ♪

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:12.610
- It does have real time
auto-focus tracking, real time.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:15.210
I auto-focus and and add a lot of focus,

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.130
which, you know,

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:19.050
we definitely use that
quite often with Maddie.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:20.340
So we're now out here in Santa Monica,

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.350
taking some photos of videos.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.050
This is where I always come
to do our test shoots because

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:25.760
it's usually a really nice view.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.260
But the air quality basically

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:31.630
in all of the West coast is
pretty terrible, today included.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:33.440
So I'm gonna try to get
you guys some footage

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.730
so you can see what this looks like,

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:36.770
but it's not very nice out today.

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:37.830
This is shooting in 4k,

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.180
and one of my favorite things
about the new updated Sony's

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:42.670
is the fast auto-focus.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.440
Are you ready Tyler?

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:45.273
Okay, ready?

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:47.613
Was it fast?

00:06:53.115 --> 00:06:53.948
(upbeat music)

00:06:53.948 --> 00:06:54.781
How's that focus?

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.253
I better put this away

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.600
before I stabbed myself or you.

00:07:02.595 --> 00:07:04.560
(gravel crunching underfoot)

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:05.393
Okay, let's do a slowmo test.

00:07:06.964 --> 00:07:09.547
(upbeat music)

00:07:19.786 --> 00:07:21.560
So this doesn't do 4K 120 or 240,

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.710
like the new the new a7S III,

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:25.810
but this still does do HD 120 and S and Q.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:28.280
So that was an example of that.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.113
What's next?

00:07:29.113 --> 00:07:30.330
Should we take some photos?

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.840
Jenna, you wanna take some photos with me?

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.840
Okay, cool.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.994
Photo test.

00:07:33.994 --> 00:07:36.577
(upbeat music)

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:49.600
Now audio is something that
you should always keep in mind

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:50.500
when creating content,

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.220
and to help you monitor that
there is a headphone jack.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.120
My favorite thing though,

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:56.060
is the built in hot shoe.

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.140
This is the XLR setup

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:58.830
that we use in almost every single video.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.660
We use the Sennheiser
AVX wireless microphones.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.090
So I'm wearing one right now,

00:08:03.090 --> 00:08:05.190
right here, hello.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:07.223
And this is going right
into the Sony a7 III

00:08:07.223 --> 00:08:08.330
that we're filming with.

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.410
This is the setup that we use
for pretty much every video

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.990
that we shoot when we're out and about

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:13.500
or sitting here at the desk.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.460
I love having a wireless mic on,

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.920
and we usually just use
the shotgun for backup.

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.760
Now, if you don't go
the wireless love route,

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.300
making sure you have a great
shotgun mic is very important.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:25.090
There are lots of options out there,

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:26.880
like some of these,

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.600
when it comes to getting
external microphones,

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.590
that's also incredibly overwhelming.

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.040
These are the two that are my go-to's

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.640
when I'm shooting with Sony cameras.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.640
This little guy is the ECM-XYST1M,

00:08:39.881 --> 00:08:40.714
this is gonna be a quiz later,

00:08:40.714 --> 00:08:41.547
so make sure you remember that.

00:08:41.547 --> 00:08:43.490
This is the one that I've been using

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:44.700
pretty much the longest.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.290
It's great because it's super small.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.650
It does have a little shock Mount.

00:08:47.650 --> 00:08:49.790
So if you are vlogging and
moving it around a lot,

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:50.900
pretty stable.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.380
The one thing that I just noticed

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.010
as I was shaking this around,

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.940
the a7S III has

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.930
these added little sound
dampening technology?

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.010
I don't know, I think it just made these

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:02.980
a little bit more stiff.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.130
But you can't hear them

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:07.020
on the camera, whereas this,

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.410
they don't have that.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:11.090
So normally what I do is
I either take these off

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.670
or I will tape them so that you don't hear

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.210
that rattling around in the
body when you're filming.

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.910
But this little microphone is great.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.480
You can do stereo.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:19.960
You can move those around

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:22.500
depending upon what you're doing.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.320
Whereas this one is the,

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.300
what kind of crazy name did they give you?

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.750
The ECM-B1M.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.680
Now this microphone I really like,

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:34.060
this one is a little bit more advanced

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:35.910
and it's also way more expensive.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:38.480
So if you are looking to cut costs,

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.020
definitely recommend this one.

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.900
Do we remember what that one was called?

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:43.380
No, I've only been using it for 6 years.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.110
Yeah, look at that.

